        <p>I once stood in front of a classroom of underserved 8th graders in New York who had no interest in learning physics. Loud, restless, testing every boundary. My job was to find a way to motivate them, not by imposing order, but by making the subject matter interesting enough to earn their attention. I've built my life around elevating human potential, working on meaningful problems related to the future of education, the future of work, our relationship with our environment, and AI.</p>
        <p>My focus on human flourishing has kept me focused on problems I keep returning to: how can we learn better, how do we live more sustainably on this planet, and how do we use technology to free people up for work that actually matters.</p>
        <p>I spent my early career at Bain working deeply in energy and semiconductors, then joined Avataar, a Series B enterprise AI company focused on automation of 3D modelling. At the Stanford GSB, I've built and scaled an AI oral assessment platform used by thousands of students, and stood up a climate risk marketplace.</p>
        <p>Outside of work I cook, cycle, surf, read, explore the outdoors and volunteer.</p>
